    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\n\u2705 **Bug Fixed!** The `frai gate init --ci` command now correctly creates the GitHub Actions workflow.\n\n### The Problem\nWhen calling `frai gate init --ci`, Commander.js was consuming the `--ci` flag at the main program level before it reached the gate subcommand. The gate command was only receiving `['init']` instead of `['init', '--ci']`, causing the workflow file not to be created.\n\n### The Solution\nModified `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 737-755) to extract arguments directly from `process.argv` instead of relying on Commander's parsed arguments. This preserves all flags and options that were passed to the gate subcommand.\n\n**Key change:**\n- Removed the `args` parameter from the action handler\n- Extract arguments using `process.argv.indexOf('gate')` to find where the gate command starts\n- Pass all arguments after `gate` to the subprocess: `process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1)`\n\n### Verification\n\u2713 Rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`  \n\u2713 Tested `frai gate init --ci` - both files now created:\n  - `FRAI-SPEC.md` \n  - `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`",
